te that there are $3$ equilibrium points, $y=-3,$ $y=1,$ and $y=4.$\n\n- We're given that $y=4$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=4$ and an upward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=1$ is a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing an upward-pointing arrow just above $y=1$ (already drawn by the above property) and a downward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=-3$ is a node. This means that the arrows on either side of $y=-3$ point in the same direction. Since the arrow just above $y=-3$ points downward, the arrow just below it points downward too.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/e428cf67a486e9eb17764727ab042bb44e07dfe4f13c125112fb56799d5aadea.png)\n\nOf the given options, the only slope field that corresponds with this phase line is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/26f65c17a5b108cc0c739bbfa5d7971841bfe71dc8886fb801e2ca5b5d2a32ae.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The slope field is horizontal at $y=-3,$ $y=1,$ and $y=4.$\n\n- The slopes near $y=-3$ appear to diverge away from this line when we're looking below the line and appear to converge toward the line when we're looking above the line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=1$ appear to diverge away from this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=4$ appear to converge toward this line." 13194139534897 true] [17592186318164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318165 13194139534897 true] [17592186318164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318166 13194139534897 true] [17592186318164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318167 13194139534897 true] [17592186318164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318168 13194139534897 true] [17592186318164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318169 13194139534897 true] [17592186318164 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534897 true] [17592186318164 1041 "selection" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318164 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318165 13194139534897 true] [17592186318164 1110 #uuid "0d368435-fd4b-5111-ab80-ab1c5d5c91a4" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318165 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/26f65c17a5b108cc0c739bbfa5d7971841bfe71dc8886fb801e2ca5b5d2a32ae.png" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318165 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534897 true] [17592186318165 1111 #uuid "24865ba0-0d9e-5112-b763-a3c03c64c4d8" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318166 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/ad543fe5e3bda9c57f298c96547e722fea5bed48a4752cac1520b9814b11fa48.png" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318166 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534897 true] [17592186318166 1111 #uuid "a5e2a673-b0fe-5d44-b820-b24e9eef6328" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318167 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/9295a422a3f393012ebeb664e1b5867483b34e7f35260994364add19a1e99b48.png" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318167 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534897 true] [17592186318167 1111 #uuid "28840676-5d5a-5de0-9fb0-73d2260a78b6" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318168 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/b0435deaf5351bf3d0c5debe40ef705b8f8b01b6fd4133a2fbca4a12034d9b91.png" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534897 true] [17592186318168 1111 #uuid "034ccd35-2ca3-5b1f-823b-a44152b00c23" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318169 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/0b8561b868005f359ec3a9d023ada261053fe04e8b3c970fc787a93faff91a5f.png" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318169 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534897 true] [17592186318169 1111 #uuid "3603925f-aba6-55de-afb0-960ba8a8d4a2" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318170 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318171 13194139534897 true] [17592186318170 1089 "q-96554" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318170 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534897 true] [17592186318170 1100 "Which of the following statements is true regarding the equilibrium solutions of ${y}^{′}={y}^{2}-3y?$" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318170 1113 #uuid "34f74b98-19b4-503e-9cba-984793f00280" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318170 1145 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we need to find the equilibrium solutions. So, we solve $f(y)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-3y & =0 \\\\ y(y-3) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equilibrium solutions are $y=0$ and $y=3.$ \n\nNow, we analyze the sign of $f(y)$ using a sign table, as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,0)$ | $(0,3)$ | $(3,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $y-3$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (3,\\infty ),$ and negative for $y\\in (0,3).$\n\nWe can now draw the phase line for this equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/09fbbcef280dc3d6c0b68e2de23643fae8cbda246863d1b1d325ccb1c6368b4d.png)\n\nFinally, we classify the equilibrium solutions:\n\n- $y=0$ is a sink.\n\n- $y=3$ is a source.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$y=0$ is a sink, and $y=3$ is a source\"." 13194139534897 true] [17592186318171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318172 13194139534897 true] [17592186318171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318173 13194139534897 true] [17592186318171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318174 13194139534897 true] [17592186318171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318175 13194139534897 true] [17592186318171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318176 13194139534897 true] [17592186318171 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534897 true] [17592186318171 1041 "selection" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318171 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318176 13194139534897 true] [17592186318171 1110 #uuid "c4ed55fa-93dd-517c-bb0e-36b8702e4fc8" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318172 1034 "$y=0$ is a sink, and $y=3$ is a node" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318172 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534897 true] [17592186318172 1111 #uuid "9167b200-5017-5758-9cbc-f4819783322c" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318173 1034 "$y=0$ and $y=3$ are both sources" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318173 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534897 true] [17592186318173 1111 #uuid "10aee039-ddd8-5bed-8b83-93a4e7b6d8b3" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318174 1034 "$y=0$ and $y=3$ are both nodes" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534897 true] [17592186318174 1111 #uuid "470f6110-8460-5960-9b96-03fce0763053" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318175 1034 "$y=0$ is a source, and $y=3$ is a sink" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534897 true] [17592186318175 1111 #uuid "bda47b26-7cb5-539e-bff4-bdcd238b7d43" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318176 1034 "$y=0$ is a sink, and $y=3$ is a source" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534897 true] [17592186318176 1111 #uuid "b680f59f-01a5-5dc4-a300-f5e189d31cbb" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318177 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318178 13194139534897 true] [17592186318177 1089 "q-98700" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318177 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534897 true] [17592186318177 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/4c4ef140c85eb91bd01688cc2a447f13a21c2a51964c6d101887d15045cee95d.png)\n\nA particular autonomous differential equation has the phase line shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=-2$ is a sink\n- $y=-2$ is a source\n- $y=2$ is a node" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318177 1113 #uuid "18d0fac2-3f3b-5fc0-81b1-b5cedbfc4a46" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318177 1145 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nLet's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=-2$ points downward, and the arrow just below it points upward. In other words, both arrows point *toward* the point $y=-2.$This means that $y=-2$ is a sink.\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=2$ points downward, and the arrow just below it points downward too. In other words, both arrows point in the *same* direction on either side of $y=2.$ This means that $y=2$ is a node.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139534897 true] [17592186318178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318179 13194139534897 true] [17592186318178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318180 13194139534897 true] [17592186318178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318181 13194139534897 true] [17592186318178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318182 13194139534897 true] [17592186318178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318183 13194139534897 true] [17592186318178 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534897 true] [17592186318178 1041 "selection" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318178 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318180 13194139534897 true] [17592186318178 1110 #uuid "2abae91b-859d-546d-8d28-dab2e012b169" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318179 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318179 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534897 true] [17592186318179 1111 #uuid "e749cb57-30c6-5395-b47b-a0225bdfcd37" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318180 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318180 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534897 true] [17592186318180 1111 #uuid "d29d8dc6-4d9d-50d1-9af3-9b56a92cb164" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318181 1034 "I only" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318181 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534897 true] [17592186318181 1111 #uuid "aa7c6b48-de2e-5567-bb55-65836844392f" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318182 1034 "III only" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318182 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534897 true] [17592186318182 1111 #uuid "1b6bee35-d330-5862-b8fd-88c16f973518" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318183 1034 "II only" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318183 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534897 true] [17592186318183 1111 #uuid "fd566b48-7f8d-5c4b-a305-4a78269892cf" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318184 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318185 13194139534897 true] [17592186318184 1089 "q-98706" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318184 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534897 true] [17592186318184 1100 "A particular autonomous differential equation has the following properties:\n\n- $y=1$ and  $y=3$ are equilibrium points\n\n- $y=3$ is a sink\n\n- $y=1$ is a source\n\nWhich of the following could be the phase line of the differential equation?" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318184 1113 #uuid "f49ad00c-219e-5dc1-970b-4f64c53ac0e5" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318184 1145 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nLet's check each condition:\n\n- We're given that $y=1$ and $y=3$ are equilibrium points. We represent this on the phase line by drawing two distinct points at these locations.\n\n- We're given that $y=3$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=3$ and an upward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=1$ is a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing an upward-pointing arrow just above $y=1$ (already drawn by the above property) and a downward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\nTherefore, our phase line is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/804857317470b8ba85edb165770e80511eaab144f76681c615625f8d5c6e8b5e.png)" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318186 13194139534897 true] [17592186318185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318187 13194139534897 true] [17592186318185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318188 13194139534897 true] [17592186318185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318189 13194139534897 true] [17592186318185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318190 13194139534897 true] [17592186318185 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534897 true] [17592186318185 1041 "selection" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318185 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318189 13194139534897 true] [17592186318185 1110 #uuid "8d9d75aa-8f0a-556c-b8ac-b71bba72c450" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318186 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042