 {y}^{2}+6y+9 & =0 \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equilibrium solution is $y=-3.$ \n\nNow, we analyze the sign of $f(y)$ using a sign table, as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-3)$ | $(3,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $(y+3)^{2}$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nWe can now draw the phase line for this equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/074ed04c41f20a891678d61a26ae06f1151299110dfd13d2c8b7f6eef3e6e363.png)\n\nFinally, we classify the equilibrium solution:\n\n- $y=-3$ is a node because it is neither a source nor a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$y=-3$ is a node\"." 13194139534897 true] [17592186318234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318235 13194139534897 true] [17592186318234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318236 13194139534897 true] [17592186318234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318237 13194139534897 true] [17592186318234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318238 13194139534897 true] [17592186318234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318239 13194139534897 true] [17592186318234 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534897 true] [17592186318234 1041 "selection" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318234 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318235 13194139534897 true] [17592186318234 1110 #uuid "c19fbb3d-1027-58c8-9c0d-fef11e4f804c" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318235 1034 "$y=-3$ is a node" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318235 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534897 true] [17592186318235 1111 #uuid "5bcf6f5e-187a-5faf-9b08-2811fdecda6f" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318236 1034 "$y=-3$ is a sink" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534897 true] [17592186318236 1111 #uuid "c6838c90-d12a-5863-96d3-0456aebfc28c" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318237 1034 "$y=-3$ is a source" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534897 true] [17592186318237 1111 #uuid "