] [17592186318248 1041 "selection" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318248 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318253 13194139534897 true] [17592186318248 1110 #uuid "b4d30067-3bc9-5d61-9151-05e62b6738a3" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318249 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/cb969282e886301360cf22a0412c7ffb8652f24f15863de275997de039f7173f.png" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318249 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534897 true] [17592186318249 1111 #uuid "94049f66-21d5-51c3-b92f-f5cbf532aaa5" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318250 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/e45b4514ad0d059aba9a65b3b19fa26d46e095e52bfe96d0950244cea5ce1129.png" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318250 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534897 true] [17592186318250 1111 #uuid "a459a994-169c-55f6-873f-56af8f248078" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318251 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/5719e8463a1eab4af647266adb6ed60a6f10e6e7115b43dee16d4c1c19deff16.png" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318251 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534897 true] [17592186318251 1111 #uuid "52a4a979-90fc-507d-b1e8-fc2529d63dd3" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318252 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/d5698261302e24daa5b7d0d482e3f139db0ebfa86d6b094189d23157aab12301.png" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318252 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534897 true] [17592186318252 1111 #uuid "b7a2c7b4-f55e-529f-94d2-0db0faeaa5c3" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318253 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/969df5fecbd590c56d2326568dd39b18582b54c129be86a4b86afc449ffedd9b.png" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318253 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534897 true] [17592186318253 1111 #uuid "bc98f865-4f91-5eac-8c7a-4e1a4c1185ee" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318254 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318255 13194139534897 true] [17592186318254 1089 "q-98814" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318254 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534897 true] [17592186318254 1100 "A particular autonomous differential equation has the following properties:\n\n- $y=-2$ is a sink\n\n- $y=-1$ is a source\n\n- $y=3$ is a node\n\nWhich of the following could be the slope field of the differential equation?" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318254 1113 #uuid "f2360fff-fd15-5336-bdf4-c3f68971846c" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318254 1145 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we draw the phase line with the given information. \n\nNote that there are $3$ equilibrium points, $y=-2,$ $y=-1,$ and $y=3.$\n\n- We're given that $y=-2$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=-2$ and an upward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=-1$ is a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing an upward-pointing arrow just above $y=-1$ and a downward-pointing arrow just below it  (already drawn by the above property).\n\n- We're given that $y=3$ is a node. This means that the arrows on either side of $y=3$ point in the same direction. Since the arrow just below $y=3$  points upward, the arrow just above it points upward too.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/6a05aa0192d5edcb3181e44a5e3c15f5514372c8c50f105e9c4bbae40d660118.png)\n\nOf the given options, the only slope field that correspond with this phase line is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/06a3d9118f9e3c09f374760a6e8209b33c9458e4d4b476c56fae3c57f2ca3fbe.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The slope field is horizontal at $y=-2,$ $y=-1,$ and $y=3.$\n\n- The slopes near $y=-2$ appear to converge toward this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=-1$ appear to diverge away from this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=3$ appear to diverge away from this line when we're looking above the line and appear to converge toward the line when we're looking below the line." 13194139534897 true] [17592186318255 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318256 13194139534897 true] [17592186318255 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318257 13194139534897 true] [17592186318255 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318258 13194139534897 true] [17592186318255 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318259 13194139534897 true] [17592186318255 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318260 13194139534897 true] [17592186318255 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534897 true] [17592186318255 1041 "selection" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318255 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318260 13194139534897 true] [17592186318255 1110 #uuid "36ec6f16-0886-589e-b305-81b9eb50a72b" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318256 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/b291a1bb92db8f61a5c73274bdb65b5a3c3316c539a30f8539fef4fc763ab75c.png" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318256 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534897 true] [17592186318256 1111 #uuid "a166494c-962a-54b0-b898-f0afe2631bd5" 13194139534897 true] [17592186318257 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/01a3f9b8882698362729a25b874994e9e4879d797efde534b3cbbc0aec9d53c4.p